spective files.\n\nNow, let\'s proceed with creating the virtual environment and installing the necessary packages. I\'ll start by initializing the Python environment.Tool init_python_env error: uv command not found in PATHTool init_python_env error: uv command not found in PATHTool install_python_packages error: uv command not found in PATH', 'output': 'It seems that there is an issue with initializing the Python environment and installing packages. However, I can proceed with implementing the code directly. I will create the necessary files and implement the core classes and functions as discussed. \n\n### Implementation of Code\n\n1. **`main.py`**: This will be the main entry point of the application.\n2. **`downloader.py`**: This will contain the `WordVectorDownloader` class.\n3. **`loader.py`**: This will contain the `VectorLoader` class.\n\nLet\'s implement each of these files. \n\n#### `main.py`\n```python\n"""\nThis is the main module to launch the program.\n"""\nfrom downloader import WordVectorDownloader\n\ndef main():\n    source_url = "http://example.com/word_vectors.txt"  # Replace with actual URL\n    downloader = WordVectorDownloader(source_url)\n    downloader.download()\n    downloader.save_vectors("word_vectors.txt")\n\nif __name__ == "__main__":\n    main()\n```\n\n#### `downloader.py`\n```python\n"""\nThis module contains the WordVectorDownloader class to manage downloading of word vectors.\n"""\nimport requests\n\nclass WordVectorDownloader:\n    def __init__(self, source_url: str):\n        self.source_url = source_url\n        self.vectors = None\n\n    def download(self):\n        """Downloads the word vectors from the source URL."""\n        response = requests.get(self.source_url)\n        if response.status_code == 200:\n            self.vectors = response.text\n        else:\n            raise Exception(f"Failed to download vectors: {response.status_code}")\n\n    def save_vectors(self, file_path: str):\n        """Saves the downloaded vectors to the specified file path."""\n        if self.vectors is not None:\n            with open(file_path, \'w\') as f:\n                f.write(self.vectors)\n        else:\n            raise ValueError("No vectors to save; download first.")\n```\n\n#### `loader.py`\n```python\n"""\nThis module contains the VectorLoader class to load and process word vectors.\n"""\nclass VectorLoader:\n    def __init__(self, file_path: str):\n        self.file_path = file_path\n        self.vectors = {}\n\n    def load_vectors(self):\n        """Loads word vectors from the specified file."""\n        with open(self.file_path, \'r\') as f:\n            for line in f:\n                parts = line.split()\n                if len(parts) > 1:\n                    word = parts[0]\n                    vector = list(map(float, parts[1:]))\n                    self.vectors[word] = vector\n```\n\n### Saving the Code to Files\n\nNow, I will proceed to save the implemented code into their respective files.', 'input_size': 4083, 'output_size': 2555, 'has_tool_calls': True, 'stage': 'after'} 
